{"id": "EUVD-2026-80589", "enisaUuid": "2800f9fa-f843-379a-b823-4e3fe6c02ffc", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nublk: clear VM_MAYWRITE on read-only ublk char device mmap\n\nublk_ch_mmap() rejects mmap requests with VM_WRITE set, but never\nclears VM_MAYWRITE on the resulting read-only mapping. This allows\na userspace daemon to mmap the per-queue command buffer PROT_READ,\nthen upgrade it to PROT_WRITE via mprotect(), since VM_MAYWRITE was\nnever cleared.\n\nThe command buffer holds struct ublksrv_io_desc entries that are\nkernel-written ABI; a writable mapping lets an unprivileged daemon\nprocess corrupt fields such as addr, op_flags, nr_sectors, and\nstart_sector.\n\nSame bug class as the drm/panthor and drm/vc4 VM_MAYWRITE fixes, and\nthe 2026-08-13 ptp/vmclock fix (a5edadbae57e).\n\nVerified via mprotect() PoC: before the fix, a PROT_READ mapping can\nbe upgraded to PROT_READ|PROT_WRITE and a write into the command\nbuffer corrupts io_desc fields (confirmed under KASAN). After the\nfix, mprotect() returns -EACCES.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T09:54:33", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:52:48", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/be41733c24be58e2a1ef718c80fafdfb98a40d5e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5befd06a72216869b607cf7724a4f16c6a2d3999", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e373c1acdbcf88cec533ece9f589020adaed0a78", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fa5e1bc673ca59722608af67b27e65dba0c97926", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6e2b571b0a54755b06e092501913e1dfefe75d6c"], "aliases": ["GHSA-fp98-h54j-vwfj", "CVE-2026-89793"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0cf48ec6-8835-3158-aaad-220840b26867", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "71f28f3136aff5890cd56de78abc673f8393cad9 <be41733c24be58e2a1ef718c80fafdfb98a40d5e"}, {"id": "19e73353-f4ec-34d7-b77c-b220c3347534", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "211dbfc4-4279-32d1-8e2f-b21ab9002dea", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "71f28f3136aff5890cd56de78abc673f8393cad9 <5befd06a72216869b607cf7724a4f16c6a2d3999"}, {"id": "49d3474c-75cd-3d9c-a312-84b9fad61299", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "4f21bc5a-1d86-3ec2-9acb-7d1759bf2605", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "71f28f3136aff5890cd56de78abc673f8393cad9 <6e2b571b0a54755b06e092501913e1dfefe75d6c"}, {"id": "67e19d71-3386-36f9-bbaf-1711c02f1e3f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "7658666d-e078-3aea-95aa-561fca700970", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}, {"id": "99f48bb5-a461-3b69-83b8-1280a5c745a4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.0"}, {"id": "bc3e842a-1fa4-3122-8f1e-54e1bef549b8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "71f28f3136aff5890cd56de78abc673f8393cad9 <fa5e1bc673ca59722608af67b27e65dba0c97926"}, {"id": "c07ead65-487d-3a23-8e70-cb1bd010adcd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "ccd0c131-3ab5-339f-aed8-e22743328714", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "f6972df2-bdcb-3247-9c58-c175a8c01e16", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "71f28f3136aff5890cd56de78abc673f8393cad9 <e373c1acdbcf88cec533ece9f589020adaed0a78"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a84089fa-6714-3b14-8f96-016f627099d7", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}